{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a detailed stitch task (Task ID 5150) to implement `cmd/du/main.go` for the go-unix-utils project. The task is specifically scoped to SRD requirements R1.1-R1.4 (the \"Default behavior\" group of srd009-du), which covers:\n   - R1.1: Recursive directory traversal and disk usage summation, defaulting to \".\" when no args\n   - R1.2: Default output in 1024-byte (1K) block units using `fi.Blocks / 2`\n   - R1.3: Tab-separated \"SIZE\\tPATH\\n\" output format\n   - R1.4: No symlink following during traversal (use Lstat)\n   - Hard link deduplication (task R4 text says \"hard link deduplication\" referencing R1.4, but SRD R3.1-R3.3 describes the actual dedup mechanism)\n   \n   Design decisions: D1 (SIGPIPE handler), D2 (use Lstat), D3 (standard flag package).\n   Acceptance criteria: AC1 (go build succeeds), AC2 (go vet passes), AC3 (recursive reporting works), AC4 (tab-separated output format).\n   Only file to create: `cmd/du/main.go`. No test file in this task.\n   Git is managed externally - no git commands allowed.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go module path: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n   - `pkg/sys.Lstat(path)` returns `*sys.FileInfo` with Blocks, Dev, Ino, Mode fields (doesn't follow symlinks)\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for SIGPIPE handling at process startup\n   - Hard link deduplication via Dev+Ino pair tracking in a map\n   - Block size conversion from 512-byte blocks (st_blocks) to 1K blocks via `Blocks / 2`\n   - Post-order directory traversal (subdirectories printed before parent)\n   - Default behavior: only directories are printed (files counted toward parent totals but not printed individually), except file arguments at the top level ARE printed\n   - SPDX copyright header required on every Go file\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max (E8)\n   - File size limit: 500 lines (E9)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd009-du.yaml` (lines 1-150)\n     - Read to understand requirements R1.1-R1.4, R2.x (flags), R3.x (hard link dedup), R4.x (exit codes), R5.x (signals), non_goals\n     - Key: R1.2 says `fi.Blocks / 2` for 1K blocks, R1.3 says \"SIZE\\tPATH\\n\" format, R1.4 says use Lstat\n     - Hard link dedup (R3.1-R3.3): track by Dev+Ino pair, per-invocation scope\n\n   - `pkg/sys/fileinfo.go` (full file)\n     - Contains FileInfo struct and Stat/Lstat functions\n     - Key code:\n     ```go\n     type FileInfo struct {\n         Mode       os.FileMode\n         Size       int64\n         Nlink      uint64\n         Uid        uint32\n         Gid        uint32\n         Rdev       uint64\n         Dev        uint64\n         Ino        uint64\n         Blocks     int64\n         Blksize    int64\n         ModTime    time.Time\n         AccessTime time.Time\n         ChangeTime time.Time\n         Info       os.FileInfo\n     }\n     func Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) { ... }\n     func Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) { ... }\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (full file)\n     - Contains InstallSIGPIPEHandler() implementation\n     ```go\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n         c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n         signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n         go func() {\n             <-c\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }()\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `go.mod` (full file)\n     - Module path: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`, Go 1.26.3, depends on `golang.org/x/sys v0.44.0`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - code hasn't been written to disk. Design phase only.\n   - Noted a potential SRD contradiction: R1.2 mentions `sys.Stat` but R1.4 and design decision D2 say to use `sys.Lstat`. Resolution: use Lstat per D2 and R1.4.\n   - Considered block rounding issue: SRD says `fi.Blocks / 2` (truncating) but GNU du uses ceiling division `(blocks + 1) / 2`. Decided to follow SRD literally with `fi.Blocks / 2`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Resolved Stat vs Lstat contradiction in favor of Lstat (per D2 and R1.4)\n   - Designed function decomposition to stay under 40-line limit per E8\n   - Determined that directories should NOT be tracked in the dedup map (only files via fileSize function)\n   - Determined that top-level file arguments should be printed, but files found during traversal should not (matching GNU du default behavior)\n   - Designed error handling: print to stderr, continue processing, track exit code\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive task prompt containing the full stitch task specification, project context, execution constitution, go style constitution, SRD content, package contracts, shared protocols, constraints, and task requirements for implementing cmd/du/main.go with requirements R1.1-R1.4.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed conversation summary.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Write `cmd/du/main.go` implementing srd009-du R1.1-R1.4\n   - Run `go build -o bin/du ./cmd/du/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/du/` to verify no warnings (AC2)\n   - Verify binary recursively reports disk usage (AC3)\n   - Verify tab-separated output format (AC4)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I completed the design phase for `cmd/du/main.go` and was about to write the file. The complete planned implementation:\n\n   ```go\n   // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n   // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n   // cmd/du implements recursive directory disk usage reporting.\n   // Implements srd009-du R1.1-R1.4.\n   package main\n\n   import (\n       \"fmt\"\n       \"os\"\n       \"path/filepath\"\n\n       \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n   )\n\n   type inodeKey struct {\n       Dev uint64\n       Ino uint64\n   }\n\n   func main() {\n       sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n       args := os.Args[1:]\n       if len(args) == 0 {\n           args = []string{\".\"}\n       }\n\n       seen := make(map[inodeKey]bool)\n       exitCode := 0\n\n       for _, arg := range args {\n           if err := processArg(arg, seen); err != nil {\n               exitCode = 1\n           }\n       }\n\n       os.Exit(exitCode)\n   }\n\n   func processArg(path string, seen map[inodeKey]bool) error {\n       fi, err := sys.Lstat(path)\n       if err != nil {\n           fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"du: %v\\n\", err)\n           return err\n       }\n\n       if !fi.Mode.IsDir() {\n           size := fileSize(fi, seen)\n           printEntry(size, path)\n           return nil\n       }\n\n       _, err = walkDir(path, fi, seen)\n       return err\n   }\n\n   func walkDir(path string, fi *sys.FileInfo, seen map[inodeKey]bool) (int64, error) {\n       entries, err := os.ReadDir(path)\n       if err != nil {\n           fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"du: %v\\n\", err)\n           size := blockSize(fi)\n           printEntry(size, path)\n           return size, err\n       }\n\n       total, firstErr := accumChildren(path, entries, seen)\n       total += blockSize(fi)\n       printEntry(total, path)\n       return total, firstErr\n   }\n\n   func accumChildren(dir string, entries []os.DirEntry, seen map[inodeKey]bool) (int64, error) {\n       var total int64\n       var firstErr error\n\n       for _, entry := range entries {\n           childPath := filepath.Join(dir, entry.Name())\n           size, err := childSize(childPath, seen)\n           if err != nil && firstErr == nil {\n               firstErr = err\n           }\n           total += size\n       }\n\n       return total, firstErr\n   }\n\n   func childSize(path string, seen map[inodeKey]bool) (int64, error) {\n       fi, err := sys.Lstat(path)\n       if err != nil {\n           fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"du: %v\\n\", err)\n           return 0, err\n       }\n\n       if fi.Mode.IsDir() {\n           return walkDir(path, fi, seen)\n       }\n\n       return fileSize(fi, seen), nil\n   }\n\n   func fileSize(fi *sys.FileInfo, seen map[inodeKey]bool) int64 {\n       key := inodeKey{Dev: fi.Dev, Ino: fi.Ino}\n       if seen[key] {\n           return 0\n       }\n       seen[key] = true\n       return blockSize(fi)\n   }\n\n   func blockSize(fi *sys.FileInfo) int64 {\n       return fi.Blocks / 2\n   }\n\n   func printEntry(size int64, path string) {\n       fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"%d\\t%s\\n\", size, path)\n   }\n   ```\n\n   Key design decisions in the code:\n   - `inodeKey` struct for Dev+Ino dedup key\n   - `processArg` handles top-level args (prints both files and dirs)\n   - `walkDir` does post-order traversal (children first, then print parent)\n   - `accumChildren` extracted to keep walkDir under 40 lines\n   - `childSize` handles per-child Lstat and recursion\n   - `fileSize` does hard-link dedup check before counting blocks\n   - `blockSize` converts 512-byte blocks to 1K: `fi.Blocks / 2`\n   - Only files go through dedup (directories call blockSize directly)\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the file `cmd/du/main.go` with the designed implementation above, then run `go build -o bin/du ./cmd/du/` and `go vet ./cmd/du/` to verify acceptance criteria AC1 and AC2. The task description states: \"files: - path: cmd/du/main.go, action: create, note: du utility -- recursive directory disk usage reporting\" and acceptance criteria require \"go build -o bin/du ./cmd/du/ succeeds with no errors\" and \"go vet ./cmd/du/ passes with no warnings\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5150/7acb8366-1609-4b90-a8f9-0534dbaa8006.jsonl\nCon